ROVA — COMPLETE UX/UI & PRODUCT EXPERIENCE REDESIGN

PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Perform a complete UX/UI and product experience redesign of the existing ROVA application.

The current application already has a foundation, features, functionality, and structure. Do not treat this as a new application and do not unnecessarily rebuild the entire project from scratch.

The goal is to significantly improve how the application feels, behaves, navigates, and communicates with users.

The application must become:

* Extremely simple to understand.
* Fast and fluid to navigate.
* Minimal, elegant, and premium.
* Mobile-first and naturally adapted to mobile devices.
* Functional without excessive menus or unnecessary screens.
* Consistent across every section.
* Easy to use without instructions or tutorials.
* More like a modern native mobile application than a traditional website.

This is not simply a visual redesign.

This is a complete experience redesign covering:

1. Product architecture.
2. UX and user journeys.
3. Navigation.
4. Screen structure.
5. UI design.
6. Interaction behavior.
7. Transitions and animations.
8. Forms and workflows.
9. Map interactions.
10. Shipment management.
11. Responsive behavior.
12. Accessibility.
13. Performance and technical consistency.

Analyze the existing application first, then improve it intelligently.

Do not remove existing features simply because their current implementation or design is inconvenient.

