03 — NAVIGATION BEHAVIOR

Completely improve the navigation behavior.

The application currently feels too much like a traditional website when clicking buttons causes abrupt page changes and unnecessary navigation.

Correct this behavior.

The user should feel that they are interacting with one continuous application.

Implement a coherent navigation system using appropriate client-side routing and persistent application layouts.

REQUIRED BEHAVIOR

* Navigation must not unnecessarily reload the entire application.
* Avoid full-page reloads when navigating between application sections.
* Avoid abrupt transitions.
* Preserve the user’s context.
* Preserve entered information whenever appropriate.
* Maintain the previous screen state when the user returns.
* Maintain relevant filters and selections.
* Use smooth and subtle transitions.
* Make the back action predictable.
* Avoid nested navigation that becomes difficult to understand.
* Prevent duplicate navigation systems from appearing simultaneously.
* Ensure navigation works correctly on mobile and desktop.

The URL may change when necessary for deep linking, direct access, browser history, and application routing.

However, URL changes must not make the user feel as though they are leaving the application or entering an entirely different website.

Use proper SPA navigation and application-level layouts.

Do not sacrifice accessibility, direct links, browser history, or security merely to hide URL changes.

