06 — NEW DELIVERY EXPERIENCE

Redesign the delivery creation experience from beginning to end.

This is one of the most important user journeys in ROVA.

Creating a delivery must feel easy, guided, and natural.

Do not create an unnecessarily complicated multi-page wizard.

Use a contextual and continuous interface.

The user must be able to see progress without feeling trapped inside a long form.

STEP 1 — PICKUP LOCATION

Allow users to:

* Search for an address.
* Search for a business or landmark.
* Use current GPS location.
* Select a location directly on the map.
* Move the map and select a precise point.
* Adjust the location manually.
* Add relevant pickup instructions.

The search field and map must work together.

STEP 2 — DESTINATION

Allow users to:

* Search for the destination.
* Select a destination on the map.
* Use a saved address.
* Add recipient details.
* Add delivery instructions.

STEP 3 — VEHICLE SELECTION

Display available vehicles in a clear and understandable format.

Each vehicle option should include:

* Vehicle image or illustration.
* Vehicle name.
* Capacity or useful cargo information.
* Relevant size or load description.
* Price when available.
* Estimated arrival or availability.
* Selection state.

Do not present technical specifications that customers do not need.

Make vehicle selection easy.

STEP 4 — DELIVERY DETAILS

Collect only the necessary information.

Examples:

* Package description.
* Cargo type.
* Quantity when required.
* Sender contact.
* Recipient contact.
* Pickup instructions.
* Delivery instructions.
* Optional notes.

Use conditional fields.

Do not display irrelevant fields for every delivery.

STEP 5 — PRICE & CONFIRMATION

Display a clear summary before confirmation.

Include:

* Pickup.
* Destination.
* Additional stops.
* Vehicle.
* Delivery details.
* Estimated price.
* Payment method.
* Important conditions.

Make the final confirmation action obvious.

