13 — RECIPIENT TRACKING EXPERIENCE

Recipients must have an extremely simple tracking experience.

A recipient should not need to create an account to track a delivery when the existing business logic allows secure public tracking.

RECIPIENT TRACKING PAGE

The recipient should see:

* Delivery status.
* Driver position when available.
* Estimated arrival.
* Relevant route.
* Delivery information.
* Contact options when authorized.

For multi-stop deliveries, each recipient must only see information relevant to their delivery.

Do not expose:

* Other recipients’ names.
* Other recipients’ phone numbers.
* Other delivery addresses.
* Unnecessary information about the entire tour.

Tracking links must be secure and use appropriate access controls.

MULTI-STOP TRACKING

When a driver is heading toward a recipient’s stop, the recipient should receive relevant notifications and see their own tracking information.

After a stop is completed, the next recipient can become the active tracking recipient according to the delivery workflow.

The merchant must retain visibility over the complete tour.

Recipients must not have access to the merchant’s full multi-stop delivery operation.

